and \code{total}, the rows read, with \code{columns} from \code{\link[=summarize_by_cell]{summarize_by_cell()}}
or \code{column} from \code{\link[=resolution_profile]{resolution_profile()}}.
\item \code{spatialkit_replicate_var_above_nugget}. Raised by
\code{\link[=kriging_adequacy]{kriging_adequacy()}}. The replicates at one location vary between
visits more than the variogram's nugget allows; their variance is used
as it is. Refit the variogram with a nugget of at least the replicate
variance. Fields: \code{within_var} and \code{nugget}.
\item \code{spatialkit_response_ceiling}. Raised by \code{\link[=resolution_profile]{resolution_profile()}}. Rows
that are not scored (no response, or a predictor missing) lowered the
ceiling on the count. The message names the bound in force. Fields:
\code{n}, \code{n_response}, \code{ceiling}, \code{ceiling_from}, \code{n_sample} and
\code{n_scored}.
\item \code{spatialkit_response_imprecise}. Raised by \code{\link[=prep_model_data]{prep_model_data()}}, and so
by every fitter and \verb{cv_*()} function, and by \code{\link[=estimate_sac_range]{estimate_sac_range()}},
\code{\link[=kriging_adequacy]{kriging_adequacy()}} and \code{\link[=select_features_forward]{select_features_forward()}}. The response lies
so far from zero that doubles there are spaced more than a millionth of
its standard deviation apart, and every mean is rounded to that
spacing. Subtract a constant from the response first. Fields: \code{spacing}
and \code{spread}.
\item \code{spatialkit_response_scale}. Raised by \code{\link[=fit_bayesian_spatial_model]{fit_bayesian_spatial_model()}}.
\code{prior} sets a prior on the response's scale, so a response far from
zero, or with a standard deviation far from 1, is handed to \pkg{brms} as
it is. See "The response's centre and scale" in
\code{\link[=fit_bayesian_spatial_model]{fit_bayesian_spatial_model()}}.
\item \code{spatialkit_rows_dropped}. Raised by \code{\link[=prep_model_data]{prep_model_data()}}, and so by
every fitter and \verb{cv_*()} function, and by \code{\link[=gp_lengthscale_bounds]{gp_lengthscale_bounds()}}.
Rows were dropped for a missing or non-finite value or for having no
location. The message gives the counts and how far the dropped rows'
mean response sits from the kept rows'. When that difference is large,
the fit is biased towards the complete rows. Fields, from
\code{\link[=gp_lengthscale_bounds]{gp_lengthscale_bounds()}}: \code{n} and \code{which}.
\item \code{spatialkit_rows_unplaced}. Raised by \code{\link[=ensure_projected]{ensure_projected()}},
\code{\link[=harmonize_crs]{harmonize_crs()}}, \code{\link[=plot_tessellation_map]{plot_tessellation_map()}}, and the other functions
that move a layer into another CRS. The target CRS cannot place a row
in full, so the row comes back empty or without those vertices. Correct
or drop those rows. Fields: \code{rows} and \code{n}.
\item \code{spatialkit_sd_overflow}. Raised by \code{\link[=summarize_by_cell]{summarize_by_cell()}}. A cell's
standard deviation is beyond the largest double, so its \verb{..sd_*} is
\code{Inf} and its standard errors and interval are \code{NA}. Divide the column
by a power of ten. Fields: \code{columns} and \code{cells}.
\item \code{spatialkit_size_not_reached}. Raised by \code{\link[=resolution_profile]{resolution_profile()}},
\code{\link[=select_resolution]{select_resolution()}} and \code{\link[=get_voronoi_seeds]{get_voronoi_seeds()}}. A size does not give
the count it asks for (fewer than two cells, or more than k-means can
place), and the nearest level is used. Fields: \code{obs_per_cell}, \code{wanted}
and \code{used}, the two counts, and \code{reason}.
\item \code{spatialkit_surface_point_off}. Raised by \code{\link[=coerce_to_points]{coerce_to_points()}}. The
point GEOS takes on a lon/lat polygon spanning more than 180 degrees of
longitude does not lie on it read on the sphere, and that point is
kept. Transform the layer to a projected CRS that holds the polygon,
and call again. Fields: \code{rows}.
\item \code{spatialkit_ties_unresolved}. Raised by
\code{\link[=assign_features_to_polygons]{assign_features_to_polygons()}}. The \code{tie_break} rule names no polygon
for some features, since the polygons are equal on every key; those
features get \code{NA}. They are kept or dropped as \code{keep_unassigned} says.
Fields: \code{n} and \code{total}.
\item \code{spatialkit_unassigned}. Raised by \code{\link[=assign_features_to_polygons]{assign_features_to_polygons()}},
\code{\link[=build_tessellation]{build_tessellation()}} and \code{\link[=create_voronoi_polygons]{create_voronoi_polygons()}}. Features fall
inside no polygon, or points or seeds lie outside every cell. Give the
cells a \code{boundary} or \code{cover} that reaches the data; \code{keep_unassigned = TRUE} keeps such features with \code{NA}. Fields: \code{n} and \code{total}.
\item \code{spatialkit_variogram_unusable}. Raised by \code{\link[=resolution_profile]{resolution_profile()}}. The
variogram gives no usable range, so \code{reliability} is \code{NA}. \code{reason}
gives the \code{rejected_reason} of \code{\link[=estimate_sac_range]{estimate_sac_range()}}. Fields: \code{reason},
\code{converged}, \code{nugget} and \code{nugget_used}.
\item \code{spatialkit_work_limit} (error). Raised by \code{\link[=resolution_profile]{resolution_profile()}} and
\code{\link[=cell_values_at]{cell_values_at()}}. A search or a fit would make more comparisons than
an option allows. The message says what to change; see
\link{spatialkit-options}. Fields: \code{work}, \code{limit} and \code{what}, and for a fit
also \code{kind}, \code{init}, \code{nstart} and \code{fnn}.
\item \code{spatialkit_xy_imprecise}. Raised by \code{\link[=assign_features_to_polygons]{assign_features_to_polygons()}},
\code{\link[=build_tessellation]{build_tessellation()}}, \code{\link[=create_voronoi_polygons]{create_voronoi_polygons()}},
\code{\link[=create_grid_polygons]{create_grid_polygons()}}, \code{\link[=clip_target_for]{clip_target_for()}}, \code{\link[=make_folds]{make_folds()}},
\code{\link[=estimate_sac_range]{estimate_sac_range()}}, \code{\link[=fit_gwr_model]{fit_gwr_model()}} and \code{\link[=residual_morans_i]{residual_morans_i()}}.
The coordinates lie so far from the origin of their CRS that doubles
there are spaced more than a millionth of the extent apart, or a
distance lies past a tie by less than that rounding. The call runs on
the rounded coordinates. Subtract a constant from the coordinates; see
"Coordinates far from the origin" in \link{spatialkit-geometry}. Fields:
\code{spacing}, and \code{extent} or \code{distance}.
\item \code{spatialkit_xy_imprecise_error} (error). Raised by \code{\link[=clip_target_for]{clip_target_for()}}.
At that rounding the buffer comes back empty or with no area. Shift the
points nearer the origin, or pass \code{boundary}.
\item \code{spatialkit_zm_dropped}. Raised by \code{\link[=ensure_projected]{ensure_projected()}},
\code{\link[=harmonize_crs]{harmonize_crs()}}, \code{\link[=coerce_to_points]{coerce_to_points()}},
\code{\link[=assign_features_to_polygons]{assign_features_to_polygons()}}, \code{\link[=get_voronoi_seeds]{get_voronoi_seeds()}},
\code{\link[=ensure_stable_poly_id]{ensure_stable_poly_id()}}, \code{\link[=predict_surface]{predict_surface()}} and
\code{\link[=area_of_applicability]{area_of_applicability()}}. A layer that mixes XY and XYZ (or XYM)
geometries came back in XY, or \code{\link[=coerce_to_points]{coerce_to_points()}} reduced geometries
that carry M in x and y. See "Mixed dimensions, Z and M" in
\link{spatialkit-geometry}. Fields: \code{rows}, the rows that carried Z or M.
}
}

\examples{
library(sf)
set.seed(1)
# Points spread evenly have no elbow.
pts <- st_as_sf(data.frame(x = 5e5 + runif(200, 0, 100),
                           y = 5e6 + runif(200, 0, 100)),
                coords = c("x", "y"), crs = 32632)

# Catch the warning by its class and read its fields.
w <- tryCatch(determine_optimal_levels(pts, max_levels = 6),
              spatialkit_no_elbow = function(w) w)
class(w)
w$k

# Let the call finish without the warning; the log line still prints
# until the console echo is off.
old <- spatialkit_quiet()
k <- suppressWarnings(determine_optimal_levels(pts, max_levels = 6),
                      classes = "spatialkit_no_elbow")
spatialkit_quiet(old)
k
}
\seealso{
\code{\link[=spatialkit_quiet]{spatialkit_quiet()}} for the console log, \link{spatialkit-options}
for the work limits, \link{spatialkit-geometry} for the rules behind the
geometry classes, and \code{vignette("troubleshooting", package = "spatialkit")} for the messages met most often.

Other options and caches:
\code{\link[=clear_grid_cache]{clear_grid_cache()}},
\code{\link{spatialkit-options}}
}
\concept{options and caches}
